{"title":"Palindrome Partitioning (Minimum Cuts)","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"You are given a string `s`. A **partition** splits `s` into consecutive, non-empty pieces that, joined in order, give back `s`. A partition is **palindromic** if every piece reads the same forwards and backwards.\n\nEach boundary between two neighbouring pieces is one **cut**. Find the **minimum number of cuts** needed to obtain a palindromic partition of `s`.\n\nA string that is already a palindrome needs `0` cuts. A partition always exists, because every single character is a palindrome.","inputFormat":"A single line containing the string `s`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the minimum number of cuts.","constraints":["1 ≤ |s| ≤ 2000","`s` consists of lowercase English letters"],"examples":[{"input":"noonabbad","output":"2","explanation":"Split into `noon`, `abba`, `d`. All three pieces are palindromes and only 2 cuts are used. One cut is not enough, since no prefix and suffix of the string are both palindromes."},{"input":"level","output":"0","explanation":"The whole string is a palindrome, so no cut is needed."},{"input":"abcd","output":"3","explanation":"No two adjacent characters are equal, so every piece must be a single character: 4 pieces, 3 cuts."}],"tests":[{"input":"a","output":"0"},{"input":"ab","output":"1"},{"input":"aa","output":"0"},{"input":"aba","output":"0"},{"input":"abc","output":"2"},{"input":"aab","output":"1"},{"input":"abab","output":"1"},{"input":"zzzz","output":"0"},{"input":"b","output":"0"},{"input":"c","output":"0"},{"input":"ba","output":"1"},{"input":"baa","output":"1"},{"input":"aaab","output":"1"},{"input":"acac","output":"1"},{"input":"aaaaa","output":"0"},{"input":"accbb","output":"2"},{"input":"bbabab","output":"1"},{"input":"aaccca","output":"1"},{"input":"ababbab","output":"1"},{"input":"ccaaaba","output":"2"},{"input":"aabaabba","output":"2"},{"input":"cabbacca","output":"2"},{"input":"bbbbbbbaa","output":"1"},{"input":"aacaacccc","out